{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa in Cooking School: Indian Food", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "On the Way Home", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Famous Structures > The Taj Mahal", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Relate information about health and healthy habits in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Pronouns One vs. Ones", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the pronouns <span class=\"italic\">one</span> (singular) and <span class=\"italic\">ones</span> (plural) to replace nouns. You often use demonstratives (this, that, these, those) with one and ones.<br>   <br>Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">There are two pies. I like <span class=\"strong\">this one</span>. It's an apple pie.</span><br><br>You can also use them after <span class=\"italic\">Which</span> in questions.<br>   <br>Example:<br> <span class=\"italic\">Which one?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Which ones?</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I have a blue pen and a red pen. Which one do you want?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have a pair of blue shoes, and a pair of red shoes. Which ones do you want?", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to crave ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have a strong desire for something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I'm craving pie. Let's go to the bakery.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about pies.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "apple pie ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with an apple filling ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My favorite is apple pie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "cherry pie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with a filling made from a small round red fruit ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: These are cherry pies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "pumpkin pie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with a filling made from a large orange fruit that grows on the ground ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We eat pumpkin pie in October.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "peach pie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with a filling made from a round juicy fruit", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We bake peach pies in the summer. We use the peaches from the tree.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "strawberry-rhubarb pie ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with a filling made from strawberries and a plant with thick red stems", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have to cook the rhubarb before we put it into our strawberry-rhubarb pie.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "chocolate cream pie", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie made with chocolate and a thick liquid that comes from milk", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our best seller is chocolate cream pie.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "divine ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "very pleasant or good ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That pie looks divine! What kind is it?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "light ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that does not contain very much fat or sugar ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Is there anything light to eat?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn4le07ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lemon meringue pie ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a pie baked with a lemon filling and topped with a fluffy 